# glTF embedded-texture extraction output (Godot writes these on every cold
# import of the model, as <glb_stem>_<image_name>.png next to the .glb).
# Listed one path per line, never as a glob, so authored art whose name happens
# to contain underscores stays visible to git. Each is a byte-identical
# duplicate of a tracked texture, so nothing references these copies:
#   scope_Material_albedo.png      == assets/models/weapon_aglc/scope_material.png
#   PSX_Battle_Rifle_T_Battle.png  == assets/models/weapon_battle_rifle/PSX_Battle_Rifle_T_Battle_Rifle.png
# (md5 955fa408d8b72bc8c3af0f9a43e57038 and 7c75d2d5831bc31f188940a5c424cdf3)
# Note: this hides the files from `git status`; it does NOT stop Godot from
# writing them or from packing them into an export.
assets/models/weapon_aglc/scope_Material_albedo.png
assets/models/weapon_aglc/scope_Material_albedo.png.import
assets/models/weapon_battle_rifle/PSX_Battle_Rifle_T_Battle.png
assets/models/weapon_battle_rifle/PSX_Battle_Rifle_T_Battle.png.import
